The size of the blocks the allocator takes from a large heap: VulkanDeviceExtras::allocatorBlockSize, given to VMA as
preferredLargeHeapBlockSize (0, the default, keeps VMA's 256 MiB). With 256 MiB a memory type's blocks grow by 32, 64,
128 and then 256 MiB, and a phone holds every byte of a block however little of it is used.

diff --git a/plume_vulkan.cpp b/plume_vulkan.cpp
